  "limitations": [
    "This is a read-only evaluation of the supplied labeled sheets and runtime summary. No source, previous ratings, other rounds, or task state was inspected.",
    "Scores are provisional. A is the normalized mean of hierarchy, typography, and surfaces; F is the normalized mean of clarity, feedback, and accessibility. Overall uses 0.4A + 0.6F, calculated before rounding. Null is used only for genuinely inapplicable component dimensions.",
    "All represented settled labels were assessed, including loading, errors, empty/populated history, custom input, expanded explanation, offline social content, and large-text variants. Matching transition samples are included in their screen assessments.",
    "Static transition samples establish visible intermediate composition, not duration, smoothness, interruptibility, or an ignored motion preference. No motion-preference hard failure is asserted from those samples alone.",
    "The supplied summary reports 144 passing layout measurements, control-bound records, 85 passing tests, selected axe scans, and a real browser drive. The underlying measurement files were not inspected; exact target sizes and contrast ratios are therefore not certified.",
    "Normal and 200% before/after action evidence is not supplied for every screen and component. Selected preset answers, focus/press states, keyboard-open forms, enabled custom submission, populated memory, outcome controls, and several social/share states are not visibly documented.",
    "No physical iPhone, native Dynamic Type, VoiceOver/TalkBack, microphone hardware, haptics, real payments, real social/auth backend, or OS share-sheet verification is established. Browser and Safari-engine checks do not substitute for these.",
    "The supplied runtime drive supports specific completed workflows, including actual HTTP reading and PNG export. It does not prove every depicted control works, all recovery boundaries pass, or every screen meets accessibility requirements.",
    "Displayed predictions and explanatory text are synthetic fixtures. Their presentation can be judged, including conflicting dates and repetitive explanation, but they establish no model quality or predictive accuracy.",
    "No completed 60fps trace or representative novice-use evidence is supplied. No 9/10 certification is warranted, and the authorized per-screen and per-component A>=9/F>=9 threshold is not met.",
    "Approach contains an apparently essential near-invisible instruction and receives an overall below 5. Sky shows primary-action overlap, but complete inaccessibility is not established. Other below-fold content is recorded as a verification gap rather than assumed unreachable.",
    "No separate modal is shown. Full-screen plans, sharing, errors, and notices are assessed as the visible surfaces provided, without inventing modal focus or dismissal behavior."
  ],
  "topFixes": [
    "Make Approach's instruction readable and its next step explicit; establish whether it advances automatically or requires input.",
    "Remove content overlap with the tab bar and give large-text forms, explanation content, and bottom actions reliable scroll and keyboard clearance.",
    "Use one consistent layout and type treatment for equivalent follow-up answers, starting with card 2.",
    "Keep essential text legible through transitions; reduce orb deformation, abrupt clipping, and background smoke competing with content.",
    "Resolve visible meaning conflicts: remaining-reading balance versus paywall exhaustion, forecast timing versus due date, and the check-in screen's missing visible outcome task.",
    "Put offline availability beside affected social actions, strengthen selected/focus states, and remove fixture implementation language from release copy.",
    "Verify exact control bounds, animated contrast, every core 200% flow, keyboard behavior, and physical assistive-technology use before raising accessibility or functional certification."
  ]
